false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[265,1138][454,1183]" /></node><node index="1" text="HOW TO SELL ONE PRODUCT DIFFERENT WAYS" resource-id="com.zhiliaoapp.musically:id/slp" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.zhiliaoapp.musically" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[0,1197][720,1320]" /><node index="2" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.ViewGroup" package="com.zhiliaoapp.musically" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[0,1320][720,1490]"><node index="0" text='#creatorsearchinsights &#10;Have you ever noticed how two businesses can sell almost the exact same thing, yet one has people happily paying more while the other keeps competing on price?&#10;&#10;The difference is often not the product.&#10;&#10;It is the story people attach to it.&#10;&#10;That is what this carousel is about.&#10;&#10;I used something as simple as a chair to show how one product can speak to four completely different buyers.&#10;&#10;One person wants a better result.&#10;&#10;Another wants relief from a problem.&#10;&#10;Someone else wants something that reflects who they are.&#10;&#10;And another wants something associated with a certain standard.&#10;&#10;Same chair.&#10;&#10;Different narrative.&#10;&#10;When you intentionally choose the right narrative, people stop seeing your product as "just another option."&#10;&#10;They begin to see it as the one that fits them.&#10;&#10;That is how positioning works.&#10;&#10;Before creating another offer, ask yourself:&#10;&#10;"Which frame fits my buyer?"&#10;&#10;You might realise you do not need a new p